"Refrigeration Compressor Identification from Two Operating Points (R22)

A R22 refrigeration compressor operating at two measured conditions.
From the two operating points, identify the compressor parameters:
  W_dot_loss_0: constant electromechanical losses [W]
  alpha: loss factor [-]
  C: clearance factor [-]
  V_s: swept volume [m3/rev]

Subcooling: 3 K, Superheat: 5 K. Speed: 3000 rpm.

SOLVER NOTE: This model requires the .initials file for reliable convergence.
Without initial values most solver configurations fail.
"

DELTAT_sc=3
DELTAT_oh=5

"Operating point 1"
T_cd_1=34
T_ev_1=-6
Q_dot_ev_1=64000
W_dot_1=16000

"Operating point 2"
T_cd_2=46
T_ev_2=0
Q_dot_ev_2=70000
W_dot_2=20000

"assumptions"
N=rpm/60
rpm=3000

"!Calculations for operating point 1"
"!Refrigeration cycle"
"evaporator"
Q_dot_ev_1=M_dot_1*(h_1_1-h_4_1)
h_1_1=ENTHALPY(R22,T=T_1_1,P=P_ev_1)
P_ev_1=PRESSURE(R22,x=0.5,T=T_ev_1)
T_1_1=T_ev_1+DELTAT_oh
h_4_1=h_3_1
h_3_1=ENTHALPY(R22,T=T_3_1,P=P_cd_1)
P_cd_1=PRESSURE(R22,x=0.5,T=T_cd_1)
T_3_1=T_cd_1-DELTAT_sc

"compressor"
W_dot_s_1=M_dot_1*(h_2_1-h_1_1)
h_2_1=ENTHALPY(R22,s=s_1_1,P=P_cd_1)
s_1_1=ENTROPY(R22,T=T_1_1,P=P_ev_1)

W_dot_1=W_dot_loss_0+(1+alpha)*W_dot_s_1

epsilon_v_1=V_dot_su_1/V_dot_s
V_dot_s=N*V_s
V_dot_su_1=M_dot_1*v_1_1
v_1_1=VOLUME(R22,T=T_1_1,P=P_ev_1)
epsilon_v_1=1-C*(r_v_1-1)
//C = 0.28
r_v_1=v_1_1/v_2_1
//r_v_1 = 2.86
v_2_1=VOLUME(R22,h=h_2_1,P=P_cd_1)

"Cycle diagram data"
h[1]=h_1_1
h[2]=h_2_1
h[3]=h_3_1
h[4]=h_4_1
P[1]=P_ev_1
P[2]=P_cd_1
P[3]=P_cd_1
P[4]=P_ev_1

"!Calculations for operating point 2"
"!Refrigeration cycle"
"evaporator"
Q_dot_ev_2=M_dot_2*(h_1_2-h_4_2)
h_1_2=ENTHALPY(R22,T=T_1_2,P=P_ev_2)
P_ev_2=PRESSURE(R22,x=0.5,T=T_ev_2)
T_1_2=T_ev_2+DELTAT_oh
h_4_2=h_3_2
h_3_2=ENTHALPY(R22,T=T_3_2,P=P_cd_2)
P_cd_2=PRESSURE(R22,x=0.5,T=T_cd_2)
T_3_2=T_cd_2-DELTAT_sc

"compressor"
W_dot_s_2=M_dot_2*(h_2_2-h_1_2)
h_2_2=ENTHALPY(R22,s=s_1_2,P=P_cd_2)
s_1_2=ENTROPY(R22,T=T_1_2,P=P_ev_2)

W_dot_2=W_dot_loss_0+(1+alpha)*W_dot_s_2

epsilon_v_2=V_dot_su_2/V_dot_s
V_dot_su_2=M_dot_1*v_1_2
v_1_2=VOLUME(R22,T=T_1_2,P=P_ev_2)
epsilon_v_2=1-C*(r_v_2-1)
r_v_2=v_1_2/v_2_2
//r_v_2 = 3.15
v_2_2=VOLUME(R22,h=h_2_2,P=P_cd_2)

"!Results"

"Identified compressor characteristics:"
"alpha=0.204 
W_dot_loss_0=2238 "


